    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0314" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4002/45–46.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-02-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 25, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 851.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy of a note
                    received to-day from the Wai-wu Pu, referring to inauguration by Russia of the
                    municipal council at Harbin, China’s protest against the same, the Russian
                    minister’s reply to the protest, and quoting at length the rejoinder of the
                    Wai-wu Pu.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                    Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d163-a1.xml" xpointer="d163-a1"/>
            </div>
